Author: CusDeb OS Team
Description: comctl32: Scale the fixed toolbar metrics to the DPI.
 The separator width, the default button padding, the vertical padding of
 list-style buttons and the drop-down arrow with its area were fixed pixel
 values. At 192 DPI the rows of the CDEX Start menu submenus, which are
 list toolbars, were cramped next to their 32 pixel icons, and the
 drop-down arrow of the file browser's Back, Forward and Views buttons was
 a dot. Scale them to the DPI of the toolbar window; 96 DPI is unchanged.
Last-Modified: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:50:00 +0300

--- a/src/dlls/comctl32/toolbar.c
+++ b/src/dlls/comctl32/toolbar.c
